  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India - Soybean supply chain development / training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smallholder agriculture in India suffers from low productivity, scarce natural resources and difficulties in accessing financial services, technologies and inputs. It is estimated that farmers&#x2019; yields are still four to five times lower than potentially achievable. The TA provides trainings to the farmers.Currently the majority of soybean in India is grown under rainfed conditions on marginal lands. To improve yields, different aspects of production could be improved. Including fertilization, irrigation, pest management, rotation and utilization of suitable and improved seeds.</narrative>
  </description>
